          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a drogaria",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a drogaria — \"the household goods shop (cleaning things, paint)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Comprei lâmpadas e sacos do lixo na drogaria. I bought light bulbs and bin bags at the household shop."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Not a chemist: medicine is at a farmácia."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "drogaria is built on droga with -aria; droga came from French drogue (EtymDB), probably from Low German droge 'dry (goods)'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
